```dart
// ── RunIdleWatchdogWindow (gh-1617) ──────────

/// One resolved run-idle watchdog window: the duration plus the
/// precedence-source label naming where it came from (AC5).
/// Hmm — reuse ResolvedProviderTimeouts? I'll return a small record-ish class:

final class RunIdleWatchdogWindow {
  final Duration window;
  final Duration floor;         // the agent's default backstop
  final bool raised;            // window > floor — a config governs
  final String sourceLabel;     // 'default' | 'global' | 'provider:<name>' | model.timeoutScopeLabel
  final Duration connectBudget?;  // explicit connect budget when configured
  final String? connectSourceLabel;
}
```

Hmm, let me simplify. Functions:

```dart
/// The effective stream-idle patience for one model (gh-1617 I1):
/// the model's request-scoped window (gh-1554's top layer) over the
/// per-URL resolution (registry entries > global > default).
({Duration window, String source}) effectiveStreamIdleForModel(Model model) {
  final scoped = model.streamIdleTimeout;
  if (scoped != null) {
    return (
      window: scoped,
      source: model.timeoutScopeLabel ?? 'model override',  // hmm
    );
  }
  final url = Uri.tryParse(model.baseUrl);
  final resolved = resolveProviderTimeouts(url: url);
  return (window: resolved.streamIdle, source: resolved.streamIdleSourceLabel);
}
```

Hmm wait — for the model-scoped case, the source label from `timeoutScopeLabel` is like "role smol override". The ticket says the source should name "global / entry override / default". timeoutScopeLabel = 'role $role override' — good enough (it's the entry override).

But wait — there's a subtlety: when the model carries a scoped window, is that the effective idle for the run watchdog? The model's scoped window rides to the ADAPTER as the request-scoped watchdog (how? via `OpenAICompletionsOptions`... let me verify the adapters read model.streamIdleTimeout). Let me check openai_completions.dart quickly.

Also the connect budget: "explicitly set" = model.connectTimeout != null || resolved.connectSource != builtIn.

```dart
/// The run-idle watchdog window for a run streaming [model] (gh-1617
/// I1): the agent's default backstop floor raised to cover the model's
/// effective stream-idle patience — max(floor, effective idle). A
/// warming-up model gets exactly the patience its config declares;
/// nothing configured keeps the floor byte-for-byte (AC3).
Duration runIdleWatchdogWindow({required Duration floor, required Duration effectiveIdle}) =>
    effectiveIdle > floor ? effectiveIdle : floor;

/// The zero-byte replay attempt budget (gh-1617 I2/AC4): how many
/// consecutive watchdog-killed zero-byte attempts the ladder allows.
/// Unset connect budget → the ladder's own bound (2). A configured
/// budget below the idle window buys no replay (1 attempt): the ladder
/// stops at the connect budget and the terminal names both values.
int zeroByteAttemptBudget({required int ladderBound, required Duration idleWindow, required bool connectBudgetSet, Duration? connectBudget}) {
  if (!connectBudgetSet || connectBudget == null) return ladderBound;
  final affordable = 1 + connectBudget.inMilliseconds ~/ idleWindow.inMilliseconds;
  return affordable.clamp(1, ladderBound);
}
```

